# Copy to .env.mock-systems next to docker-compose.mock-systems.yml, in /srv/agents/mock-systems (RUNBOOK.md, step 6, "Run the mock service"). The copy has mode 600 on the host.
# Names and placeholders only: this example holds no key, no secret and no usable token.
# The copy holds one secret, the operator token, and it never enters git: the .gitignore of the repository covers .env.* except *.example.
# The service holds no key and no wallet. It keeps the data of its tenants in memory, so it has no volume.
# The service reads each setting one time, at start. A value that breaks a rule stops the start, and the error names the variable. The error never shows the token.
# The container reads this file when it is created. After a change, create the container again (RUNBOOK.md): restart does not read the file again.
# The two hosts of the mock systems (README.md, "The two mock host names"). Both are required. Each value is an https origin: https://, one host name, and no path.
# The service tells the two hosts apart by the Host header of a call. So each value must name the same host as its block in Caddyfile.mock-systems.snippet, and the two must be two different hosts.
# A call that names another host gets 421.
# MOCK_PUBLIC_BASE: the normal HTTPS host. Callers send access tokens and JWT-SVIDs here. The resource of a route is <this origin>/t/<tenant>/<system>.
MOCK_PUBLIC_BASE=<https origin of the mock host>
# MOCK_MTLS_BASE: the client-certificate host. Callers present an X.509-SVID as the TLS client certificate here. The service reads the Client-Cert header on this host only.
MOCK_MTLS_BASE=<https origin of the mock mtls host>
# MOCK_OPERATOR_TOKEN: required, no default. The token of POST /admin/tenants, the call that makes a tenant or makes it again. It has 32 to 128 characters of letters, digits and . _ ~ + / = -.
# Empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without it. This command makes a token of 48 letters and digits and writes it into the line below, in the copy. It prints nothing:
#   sed -i "s|^MOCK_OPERATOR_TOKEN=.*|MOCK_OPERATOR_TOKEN=$(tr -dc 'A-Za-z0-9' </dev/urandom | head -c 48)|" .env.mock-systems
# The token stays on this host. Never paste it into a chat, a ticket or a log. If the token stands in another line of this file, the service stops at start and names that line.
MOCK_OPERATOR_TOKEN=
# The identity registry deployment. The delegation check and the approval check read the ledger with it. The three lines hold the values that the identity registry deployment on Vector mainnet published on 2026-11-03.
# All three are required, so that a value with a typo stops the start: a read of the ledger with the wrong deployment finds no delegation, and the service would refuse every call.
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT (the Merkle root of the adoption allowlist, 64 hex characters) and VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED (the seed output of the configuration seal, <txid>#<index>) are the two deployment values, under the names the MCP server reads.
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_POLICY_ID: the policy ID of the identity registry, 56 lowercase hex characters, as its deployment publishes it. It must be the policy that the two values give.
# The env examples of the agents in deploy/host hold the same values: VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT and VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED in .env.advocate.example, and IDENTITY_POLICY_ID in each of the four examples.
VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT=<64 hex characters>
VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED=<txid>#<index>
VECTOR_IDENTITY_POLICY_ID=<56 hex characters>
# The services that the checks read. Each line is empty here, and an empty line keeps the default of the code. Set a line only to use another service. Each value is an https origin.
# IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL: the identity gateway. The service checks tokens and SVIDs against it. Default: https://id.vector.apexfusion.org
IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL=
# VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL: the node of the ledger that the delegation check and the approval check read. Default: https://ogmios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL=
# VECTOR_KOIOS_URL: the indexer of the ledger that the delegation check and the approval check read. Default: https://v2.koios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_KOIOS_URL=
# PORT and HOST: where the service listens inside the container. The code defaults are 9120 and 127.0.0.1. The container needs 9120 and 0.0.0.0: the compose file publishes 127.0.0.1:9120:9120.
# The compose file sets the same two values, and its values win over this file. A change here has no effect.
PORT=9120
HOST=0.0.0.0
